From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yao Xiao <yaoxia@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:21:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M156 Merge] [AdTracker] Don't run page-installed
 getters/traps in monkey-patch check

Problem:
The monkey-patch check reads properties of page-controlled objects
(e.g. `Node.prototype.appendChild`) under a
`DisallowJavascriptExecutionScope`. That scope only blocks JavaScript,
but native functions (e.g. DOM APIs) that page script installs as
getters or `Proxy` traps still run. Since the check can run while script
is forbidden (e.g. during DOM insertion), they can mutate the DOM
re-entrantly, causing use-after-free crashes.

Solution:
Do these reads with the new `v8::Object::TryGetWithNoSideEffects()`
instead, which never calls accessor getters, `Proxy` traps or
interceptors. A read that would need one is handled as if the property
were missing, e.g. the API is then treated as not monkey patched.

Since `window.history` is an accessor property, the history APIs are now
looked up directly on the window's `History` object, which is what
`window.history` returns unless page script redefined it.

(cherry picked from commit 4587ed9e4c6f8aa969ea6717f2dfcf695fb3f3d6)

